A6. Split Temporary Variable
Problem:
You have a local variable that is assigned more than once, but it is not a loop variable or a
collecting variable.
Solution:
Make a separate temporary variable for each assignment. Each temp should be assigned
only once.
When a temp is used for two different things, it can be very confusing to the reader. Use a separate
variable for each purpose.
// Before
double temp = 2 * (height + width);
System.out.println(temp);
temp = height * width;
System.out.println(temp);
// After
double perimeter = 2 * (height + width);
System.out.println(perimeter);
double area = height * width;
System.out.println(area);
CEN206 Object-Oriented Programming
RTEU CEN206 Week-13
