D4. Remove Control Flag
Problem:
You have a boolean variable that acts as a control flag for a series of conditional
expressions.
Solution:
Use
break
or
return
instead of the control flag.
// Before
boolean found = false;
for (Person p: people) {
if (!found) {
if (p.getName().equals("Don")) {
sendAlert();
found = true;
}
// After
for (Person p: people) {
if (p.getName().equals("Don")) {
sendAlert();
break;
}
CEN206 Object-Oriented Programming
