E14. Replace Exception with Test
Problem:
You throw an exception in a place where a simple test would do.
Solution:
Replace the exception with a conditional test.
// Before
double getValueForPeriod(int periodNumber) {
try {
return values[periodNumber];
} catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
return 0;
}
// After
double getValueForPeriod(int periodNumber) {
if (periodNumber >= values.length) return 0;
return values[periodNumber];
}
Exceptions should be used for unexpected conditions, not for regular flow control. A simple
if
check
is far more readable and performant than a
try/catch
